A.EP=new B.bU(A.b2X,["Phase B: explain the shape and function of the five senses.","Phase B: analyse the life cycles of living things and how to conserve them.","Phase B: draw conclusions about how matter changes state.","Phase B: explain sources and forms of energy, and how energy changes form in everyday life.","Phase B: tell apart types of force and their effect on the direction, motion and shape of objects.","Phase B: classify different landscapes and how they relate to local jobs and cultures, and how to conserve them.","Phase B: come up with solutions to problems in conserving natural resources, as a way of mitigating climate change.","Phase B: come up with solutions to problems in conserving natural resources, as a way of mitigating climate change. Context: weather as the starting point for understanding climate (weather is not named explicitly in the curriculum outcomes).","Phase C: reflect on the human body's organ systems and link them to ways of keeping the body healthy.","Phase C: analyse how the living and non-living parts of an ecosystem relate to each other, and how they affect the ecosystem.","Phase C: explain sound and light waves in everyday life.","Phase C: explain the solar system and how it relates to the Earth's rotation and revolution.","Phase C: come up with ways to save energy and to use alternative energy from local resources, as a way of mitigating climate change.","Not named explicitly in the 2025 science curriculum outcomes. Related Phase C clause: explain where Indonesia lies and its geography, using paper or digital maps.","Not named explicitly in the 2025 science curriculum outcomes. Electricity links to the energy clauses (Phase B: sources and forms of energy; Phase C: saving energy). Magnets are not named in the curriculum outcomes or the 2025 science subject guide; the nearest link: magnets in generators (hydroelectric, wind turbines) connect to the Phase C clause on using alternative energy sources.","Not named explicitly in the 2025 science curriculum outcomes. Related Phase B clause: draw conclusions about changes of state (evaporating, condensing).","Enrichment \xb7 extends the Phase B outcome on changes of state (crystallising is listed in the 2025 science subject guide)."],t.li)
